1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:06,513
This film examines the
development of a modern theme park

2
00:00:06,523 --> 00:00:10,123
featuring unusually
realistic attractions.

3
00:00:10,582 --> 00:00:14,754
A wealthy businessman develops
an ambitious new entertainment

4
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:19,247
facility combining family
recreation, scientific innovation,

5
00:00:19,257 --> 00:00:23,443
and several animals previously
considered unavailable.

6
00:00:23,892 --> 00:00:26,232
Before opening, all essential

7
00:00:26,242 --> 00:00:29,076
systems are carefully inspected.

8
00:00:29,086 --> 00:00:31,737
The fences are secure.

9
00:00:31,747 --> 00:00:34,164
The gates are locked.

10
00:00:34,174 --> 00:00:36,127
And the electrical supply

11
00:00:36,137 --> 00:00:39,027
is expected to continue existing.

12
00:00:39,554 --> 00:00:43,241
A minor staffing matter leads
to a temporary reduction in

13
00:00:43,251 --> 00:00:46,957
electricity, communications,
and the traditional

14
00:00:46,967 --> 00:00:50,386
distinction between
attractions and visitors.

15
00:00:50,848 --> 00:00:55,264
The project successfully
demonstrates that prehistoric life

16
00:00:55,274 --> 00:00:56,796
can be recreated.

17
00:00:56,806 --> 00:01:01,143
It also provides valuable
evidence that commercial viability

18
00:01:01,153 --> 00:01:03,357
and scientific possibility are

19
00:01:03,367 --> 00:01:05,659
not always close relatives.

20
00:01:06,324 --> 00:01:10,715
Several useful lessons have
therefore been identified.

21
00:01:10,936 --> 00:01:15,080
Traditional attractions
include Ferris wheels,

22
00:01:15,090 --> 00:01:17,723
carousels, and park trains.

23
00:01:17,733 --> 00:01:19,778
Dinosaurs should generally be

24
00:01:19,788 --> 00:01:22,894
considered an advanced
management option.

25
00:01:23,406 --> 00:01:25,438
Modern facilities depend

26
00:01:25,448 --> 00:01:28,251
on reliable electrical systems.

27
00:01:28,261 --> 00:01:32,289
This is particularly important
when electricity is the main

28
00:01:32,299 --> 00:01:35,129
reason the visitors
are not being eaten.

29
00:01:35,636 --> 00:01:39,320
Employees should receive
appropriate support, clear

30
00:01:39,330 --> 00:01:42,893
communication, and
adequate compensation.

31
00:01:42,903 --> 00:01:46,122
A dissatisfied employee
may reduce morale,

32
00:01:46,132 --> 00:01:48,446
productivity, and the number

33
00:01:48,456 --> 00:01:51,065
of functioning electric fences.

34
00:01:51,586 --> 00:01:55,747
The ability to do something does
not necessarily mean that it

35
00:01:55,757 --> 00:01:56,858
should be done.

36
00:01:56,868 --> 00:02:00,808
This principle is useful in
science, business, and the

37
00:02:00,818 --> 00:02:04,544
management of large
carnivorous attractions.

38
00:02:05,064 --> 00:02:08,218
This concludes today's programme.

39
00:02:08,228 --> 00:02:12,509
Please remain calm, follow
all posted instructions,

40
00:02:12,519 --> 00:02:15,659
and avoid unnecessary innovation.

41
00:02:15,669 --> 00:02:17,294
Distribution of future

42
00:02:17,304 --> 00:02:20,204
materials requires subscription.

43
00:02:20,214 --> 00:02:22,772
Thank you for your attention.

